   </dc:creator>
   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">NEW YORK, NEW YORK - SEPTEMBER 22: Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney speaks at a United Nations (UN) General Assembly meeting organized by France and Saudi Arabia in support of a two-state solution between Palestine and Israel as world leaders arrive for the 80th session of the UNâ€™s General Assembly (UNGA) on September 22, 2025 in New York City. France is expected to be the latest country to recognize the state of Palestine. Israel and the United States will boycott the summit. This yearâ€™s theme for the annual global meeting is: â€œBetter together: 80 years and more for peace, development and human rights.â€ Gaza and Ukraine are just two of the global emergencies that world leaders will look to address. (Photo by Spencer Platt/Getty Images)</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
